// The shape of a C-block's mouth. Along the side of the lines inside an if or a
// while runs an arm (its top is kept in the cursor, per level of indent, from
// the header or the else above it), and below the last line a cap closes it.
// bke_lay_caps closes as many levels as the next line leaves: the indent the
// previous line was effectively at, minus the next line's, minus one more for
// an else (which continues the if instead of closing it) and one more for the
// function's hat (which has no cap).

